WEBVTT

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:13.320
New Year's is great!

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:15.800
The kadomatsu looks so cool!

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:19.700
Miyauchi

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:26.170
Happy New Year 
I look forward to spending
another year together 
January 1 
Hotaru

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:27.750
Happy New Year 
Koshigaya Komari

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:29.500
<b>Happy New Year
Natsumi</b>

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:30.550
<b>New Year's Greetings
I appreciate everything you have done for me in the past year.
I pray for our continued friendship in the coming year.
Koshigaya</b>

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:58.530
<b>Nonstop</b>

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:09.480
<b>Episode 10</b>

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:09.480
<b>It Got Cold and Then Hot</b>

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:11.650
Nee-chan!

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:12.970
I brought New Year's cards for all of you.

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:15.560
Seriously! I need my New 
Year's money! Please!

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:16.170
Hey...

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:19.110
I spent the whole year counting on 
getting New Year's money from you,

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:20.890
and I <i>really</i> need it now!

00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:23.280
I won't get through the winter without it!

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:27.480
Come on, Renge's watching 
you. Stop acting like this.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:30.620
Renge! Help me beg for New Year's money!

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:32.120
Sigh...

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:35.100
Why do you look creeped out?! 
It's <i>New Year's money</i>!

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:40.550
<b>New
Year's
Allowance</b>

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:40.550
Yeah!

00:02:40.550 --> 00:02:42.070
Thanks, Nee-chan!

00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:43.800
Thanks, Nee-nee.

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:48.300
Now I can buy a crêpe on 
my way home from school.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:50.750
I'm gonna buy some candy 
from the candy store!

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:52.050
The candy store, huh?

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:57.930
Candy Store!

00:02:58.120 --> 00:02:59.030
Gimme—

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:05.990
Know what? I got my New Year's money, 
so I'm here to buy some candy.

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:08.070
Yeah? Good for you.

00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:14.200
Hey! I didn't even finish asking 
you for New Year's money!

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:17.410
I thought you were gonna say, 
"Gimme a faceful of your counter."

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:20.330
Then I'll try again! Gimme New Year's money!

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:24.970
Look, I'm not well off enough to 
throw around money like that.

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:27.650
Hika-nee, you shouldn't be too demanding.

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:31.350
Candy Store has it rough 
just running the store.

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:33.310
And I want these, please.

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:36.360
You don't want New Year's money, Renge?

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:39.780
I got mine from Nee-nee, so I'm good.

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:41.740
<b>New Year's Allowance</b>

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:41.740
<b>To
Renge</b>

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:42.150
I see...

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:46.330
<b>To
Renge</b>

00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:44.900
I got my candy, so I'll go home now.

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:45.960
Huh?

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:50.230
Bye, Candy Store. I'll be back soon.

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:51.930
A-All right.

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:57.170
I'm gonna eat my candy at home.

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:58.250
Yeah, sure.

00:03:58.250 --> 00:03:59.810
Hey, Renge!

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:04.810
I do have New Year's money 
for you, actually...

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:22.130
Uh, then... I'd like mine, too, please.

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:27.440
I got money from Candy Store, too! Sweet!

00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:31.170
Hika-nee, you shouldn't be too greedy.

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:34.840
Well, I won't demand it so 
obviously at the next stop.

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:41.240
Greetings, Aunt Yukiko! Happy New Year!

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:46.980
Um, Happy New Year.

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:49.150
You're awfully full of vigor today.

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:51.680
Not at all! This is how I always am!

00:04:52.030 --> 00:04:54.660
Oh... I get it.

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:57.010
You want New Year's money.

00:04:57.750 --> 00:04:58.600
There.

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:02.340
Heya, people. HNY.

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:05.140
Oh, Hika-nee. Happy New Year.

00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:06.620
Long time no see, Hikage-chan.

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:08.030
'Sup?

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:11.970
Hey! You already got New Year's money!

00:05:13.010 --> 00:05:15.280
Aunt Yukiko gave it to me.

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:18.480
Hika-nee's been real greedy today.

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:20.170
She didn't just beg Aunt Yukiko.

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:23.320
She begged Nee-nee and Candy Store, too.

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:26.840
Konomi-nee, help me set her straight!

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:30.650
Well, it's normal for adults 
to give kids New Year's money,

00:05:30.650 --> 00:05:34.380
and it would be rude to give it 
back once she's received it.

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:38.240
That's right. I guess Renge 
wouldn't understand that yet.

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:42.600
Still, Kaede-chan's old enough to 
give out New Year's money now, huh?

00:05:42.970 --> 00:05:46.070
Maybe I should start giving some, too...

00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:46.990
Oh?!

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:50.060
If you have some to give, 
I'll happily accept it!

00:05:50.060 --> 00:05:51.820
I don't have an envelope for it,

00:05:51.820 --> 00:05:53.370
but here, Hikage-chan.

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:55.570
Wow! You're serious?

00:05:55.570 --> 00:05:58.780
Sweet! I got more New Year's 
money than I thought!

00:05:58.780 --> 00:06:01.800
Now I can live like the Tokyo bourgeoisie!

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:04.740
Aw, man. I gave someone New Year's money.

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:07.390
I'm not giving it back now, even if you ask!

00:06:07.390 --> 00:06:10.150
Oh, sure, that's fine. I just meant...

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:13.900
I'm just a high school third-year, 
not a grown-up,

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:17.100
and I gave you, a first-year, 
New Year's money.

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:17.970
Huh?

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:24.190
Which means, as a first-year, you should 
give the middle school kids New Year's money.

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:29.170
Actually, I'll just give this back to you.

00:06:29.170 --> 00:06:33.030
What? You're returning a gift I gave to you?

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:35.750
Didn't I just say that would be rude?

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:41.410
Go on. You need to give the 
others some New Year's money.

00:06:43.310 --> 00:06:44.850
Yay!

00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:46.500
Thanks for the money!

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:50.370
My Tokyo bourgeoisie lifestyle!

00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:51.990
Was that good, Renge-chan?

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:54.490
I knew I could count on you, Konomi-nee!

00:06:55.140 --> 00:07:01.150
<b>Non Non Biyori</b>

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:04.640
Hika-nee! Let's go play outside!

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:07.770
Huh? Are you crazy? It's cold outside.

00:07:07.770 --> 00:07:09.290
What are you talking about?

00:07:09.290 --> 00:07:12.860
Kids are outdoor creatures. 
Cold doesn't bother us.

00:07:13.030 --> 00:07:17.730
Yeah, but I'm not a kid, and I don't 
recall being born outdoors...

00:07:17.730 --> 00:07:21.980
What the heck? 
You're shorter than me, though.

00:07:21.980 --> 00:07:24.580
And I'm not gonna let you bait me like that.

00:07:24.770 --> 00:07:26.600
You're almost never home!

00:07:26.600 --> 00:07:29.590
Stop complaining and play with us!

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:31.420
Play with us!

00:07:31.990 --> 00:07:33.510
Ow! Ow!

00:07:33.510 --> 00:07:36.270
Okay, fine! Stop pulling on me!

00:07:37.880 --> 00:07:39.610
You guys are hopeless.

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:42.940
At least it's daytime, so it 
might still be kinda warm...

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:55.980
It's snowing like crazy!

00:07:55.980 --> 00:08:00.160
C'mon, Hika-nee. You're way too 
excited over a little snow.

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:04.330
I'm not excited! I'm the exact opposite! 
That's why I shouted!

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:09.600
It's so cold... I can't play 
outside in a blizzard like this.

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:10.600
I'm going in.

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:12.460
Wait, Hika-nee!

00:08:12.870 --> 00:08:14.930
Huh? What now?

00:08:14.930 --> 00:08:19.410
I think if we move around a lot, 
we'll warm right up!

00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:21.820
Move around with us, Hika-nee!

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:24.510
Oh, good idea. 
What should we do, Ren-chon?

00:08:25.630 --> 00:08:27.200
Let's see...

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:29.540
Could you not just assume I'm in on this?

00:08:29.540 --> 00:08:33.000
I know! We'll play Daruma-san Fell Down!

00:08:33.290 --> 00:08:35.050
Okay, Hika-nee, you're up.

00:08:35.050 --> 00:08:35.690
Huh?

00:08:36.010 --> 00:08:37.450
I'm up for what?

00:08:42.630 --> 00:08:46.000
Daruma-san... fell down!

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:50.370
Daruma-san...

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:53.600
Hey! I'm not even moving at all!

00:08:53.870 --> 00:08:56.630
We're supposed to be moving 
around to warm up,

00:08:56.630 --> 00:08:58.630
but I don't even get to move a—

00:08:59.160 --> 00:09:02.190
Okay! You guys can move now!

00:09:02.410 --> 00:09:04.640
That's game, set, and match on this plan!

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:08.100
Aw, but I was starting to feel pretty warm.

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:10.660
Well, of course! You guys get to move!

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:13.100
We weren't moving that much.

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:14.760
Did you even look at us?

00:09:14.760 --> 00:09:17.870
No! If I was, that would 
be game, set, and match!

00:09:18.050 --> 00:09:19.840
I just realized something.

00:09:19.840 --> 00:09:21.560
Oh, did you now, Renge-dono?

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:27.460
I think giving Hika-nee a chance to make 
comebacks will warm her up faster than moving!

00:09:27.690 --> 00:09:28.570
Huh?

00:09:28.570 --> 00:09:30.870
Look, you're short of breath already.

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:32.990
That proves your body's warmer.

00:09:32.990 --> 00:09:33.910
I get it!

00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:39.890
So if we looked at her using thermography, 
she'd be in the light blue range!

00:09:39.890 --> 00:09:42.100
I was all blue to begin with!

00:09:42.380 --> 00:09:44.860
Wow, looking good!

00:09:44.860 --> 00:09:46.880
The light blue is turning to emerald green!

00:09:46.880 --> 00:09:49.570
At least give me a nice, healthy yellow!

00:09:49.570 --> 00:09:50.940
Dark blue.

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:52.180
Don't lower it even more!

00:09:52.390 --> 00:09:55.810
Also, what's with your fingers? 
Is that supposed to be a thermo reader?

00:09:55.810 --> 00:09:59.220
I'm sorry, ma'am. 
We're all out of salmon.

00:09:59.220 --> 00:10:00.660
You're a fishmonger now?

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:02.670
I can't even come up with comebacks anymore.

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:06.930
Translucent.

00:10:06.930 --> 00:10:08.640
Now I'm losing <i>all</i> color?!

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:10.780
The thermo's only picking up half of it!

00:10:10.780 --> 00:10:13.170
I see. Translucent.

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:15.260
Wait, what? What are you doing?

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:17.970
Filling out your record. 
Your patient record.

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:22.290
You seem to have an illness that 
makes you turn translucent,

00:10:22.540 --> 00:10:24.160
so you should come to our hospital.

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:25.880
I'm not translucent, okay?!

00:10:25.880 --> 00:10:27.310
Also, weren't you just a fishmonger?!

00:10:27.310 --> 00:10:29.540
Now, don't worry about a thing.

00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:31.870
We specialize in translucence.

00:10:31.870 --> 00:10:33.160
We have an attached 
convenience store, you see.

00:10:33.160 --> 00:10:35.320
Don't describe it like a hospital 
attached to a university!

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:36.770
Rattle, rattle.

00:10:36.770 --> 00:10:38.150
Oh, Director!

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:40.530
Wait, what? This is still going?

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:42.890
Scalpel!

00:10:42.890 --> 00:10:45.260
Already?! You guys move fast!

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:48.390
No operation ever starts <i>that smoothly!</i>

00:10:48.390 --> 00:10:50.140
There are steps leading up to it!

00:10:50.140 --> 00:10:52.280
That's true, I guess.

00:10:52.280 --> 00:10:54.780
Okay, I'll take your temperature.

00:10:54.780 --> 00:10:56.440
This is a thermometer.

00:10:56.440 --> 00:10:57.350
Yeah, yeah.

00:10:57.570 --> 00:11:00.400
Beep, beep! Your temperature is recorded.

00:11:00.400 --> 00:11:02.880
You're still moving too fast. 
All I did was take it from you.

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:05.960
What is the patient's temperature, Director?

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:08.470
This is...

00:11:11.740 --> 00:11:12.810
too far away!

00:11:12.810 --> 00:11:13.770
Far away?!

00:11:14.030 --> 00:11:15.520
What does that even mean?!

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:17.860
That's not something you say 
after taking a temperature!

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:20.470
How far away is it, Director?

00:11:20.470 --> 00:11:22.390
About as far as the Pacific.

00:11:22.390 --> 00:11:23.990
That's not even that far, is it?

00:11:23.990 --> 00:11:28.270
I see. So about the same as a 
house on a fifty-year loan.

00:11:28.270 --> 00:11:30.370
Whoa, that repayment date 
is far off, all right...

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:35.160
Hmm... Your temperature's far away, 
and you're colorless and see-through...

00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:37.080
Hika-nee, you'll have to be admitted.

00:11:37.080 --> 00:11:39.740
Not colorless and transparent! 
I'm translucent!

00:11:39.740 --> 00:11:41.350
Wait, no! I'm not translucent, either!

00:11:41.350 --> 00:11:44.100
Okay, Hika-nee, your room is right here.

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:45.360
You're just being random...

00:11:45.360 --> 00:11:48.100
This is a shared room, by the way.

00:11:49.010 --> 00:11:50.830
From the left, the other patients are...

00:11:50.830 --> 00:11:53.160
Horse Mackerel, Mackerel, 
Amberjack, and Young Amberjack.

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:54.060
Those are fish!

00:11:54.060 --> 00:11:56.500
All the patients in this room are fish!

00:11:56.500 --> 00:12:00.130
You said this was a hospital room, 
but is it actually a fish store?

00:12:00.130 --> 00:12:02.160
What you said earlier made 
it sound that way, too.

00:12:02.160 --> 00:12:04.790
I'm not sure what you're 
talking about, ma'am...

00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:08.280
So, Hika-nee, is the bed comfortable?

00:12:08.280 --> 00:12:10.890
Oh, I'm already in the bed?

00:12:11.270 --> 00:12:14.620
Uh, well, yeah... I guess it's comfortable.

00:12:14.620 --> 00:12:16.800
Isn't it, though?

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:19.190
We keep the temperature just perfect.

00:12:19.190 --> 00:12:22.590
We use the best filters and 
high-quality seawater, too.

00:12:22.590 --> 00:12:23.960
It's a fish tank now?!

00:12:23.960 --> 00:12:25.520
Rattle, rattle.

00:12:24.850 --> 00:12:26.050
Oh, Director!

00:12:26.050 --> 00:12:27.390
Time to operate!

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:29.680
What? Wait, this is my hospital room...

00:12:31.570 --> 00:12:32.790
Slice!

00:12:32.790 --> 00:12:35.660
Fantastic filleting of that amberjack, Boss!

00:12:37.250 --> 00:12:37.890
Hey!

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:40.110
This really is a fish store!

00:12:40.110 --> 00:12:43.800
And those fish aren't patients! 
They're goods on display!

00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:46.280
H-How can you say that?!

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:50.960
Calling our patients "goods" 
is making a mockery of us!

00:12:50.960 --> 00:12:52.930
Never say that again!

00:12:52.930 --> 00:12:55.910
What, so you just filleted 
a patient? Are you nuts?!

00:12:55.910 --> 00:12:59.080
And Hika-nee, how long are you 
gonna stay in that tank?!

00:12:59.080 --> 00:13:00.340
Get out of there already!

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:01.750
You put me in here!

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:06.660
Ugh! You can't even decide whether 
this is a hospital or a fish store!

00:13:06.660 --> 00:13:07.640
Make up your mind!

00:13:08.630 --> 00:13:11.500
Hospital? Fish store?

00:13:12.070 --> 00:13:15.110
This is just a convenience store, ma'am.

00:13:15.110 --> 00:13:18.350
What kind of convenience store 
is this?! I'm done here!

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:22.220
Thank you.

00:13:22.220 --> 00:13:24.250
We appreciate your patronage.

00:13:33.810 --> 00:13:36.980
What are those three doing 
out there in this blizzard?

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:43.510
<b>Nonstop</b>

00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:48.300
Miyauchi

00:14:04.060 --> 00:14:06.130
Oh, good timing.

00:14:06.130 --> 00:14:08.550
You've got a phone call.

00:14:12.420 --> 00:14:14.150
Hello?

00:14:33.010 --> 00:14:35.390
Renge-chan! Good to see you again!

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:36.810
Honoka-chin!

00:14:37.440 --> 00:14:39.510
When did you come back?

00:14:39.510 --> 00:14:43.690
Yesterday. I'm visiting my 
grandma for New Year's.

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:46.350
Oh, then let's go somewhere to play!

00:14:46.350 --> 00:14:49.110
I'll show you lots more places 
you didn't see last time!

00:14:49.110 --> 00:14:51.290
Really? Okay, let's go!

00:14:55.270 --> 00:14:58.080
Your hair accessories are cute.

00:14:58.780 --> 00:15:00.920
Yeah! They're my favorite!

00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:09.340
Oh, hey, Renge.

00:15:10.110 --> 00:15:11.390
Who's that behind you?

00:15:11.910 --> 00:15:13.260
Nice to meet you.

00:15:13.260 --> 00:15:14.580
This is Honoka-chin.

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:17.670
She's visiting her grandma 
over winter break.

00:15:18.920 --> 00:15:21.140
Look at all the different snacks!

00:15:21.140 --> 00:15:24.100
I always buy my snacks here.

00:15:34.520 --> 00:15:37.270
By the way, when are you going back home?

00:15:37.270 --> 00:15:38.200
The day after tomorrow.

00:15:39.220 --> 00:15:40.650
I see.

00:15:41.370 --> 00:15:43.620
You're not staying very long, huh?

00:15:43.860 --> 00:15:46.870
I told them I wanted to stay longer,

00:15:46.870 --> 00:15:50.210
but they said it can't be very 
long, since it's winter break.

00:15:52.730 --> 00:15:54.860
Oh, those are really good.

00:15:54.860 --> 00:15:56.050
What? Which ones?

00:15:56.300 --> 00:15:59.790
They're kinda like sweet yogurt.

00:15:59.790 --> 00:16:02.010
These? Okay, I'll buy some!

00:16:02.380 --> 00:16:03.690
I'd like these, please.

00:16:03.690 --> 00:16:04.730
Thanks.

00:16:10.520 --> 00:16:11.700
It <i>is</i> good!

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:12.600
Right?

00:16:17.430 --> 00:16:19.130
Where are we going next?

00:16:19.130 --> 00:16:20.190
Well...

00:16:20.190 --> 00:16:22.820
Careful getting home. There's a lot of snow.

00:16:22.820 --> 00:16:23.930
'Kay!

00:16:31.070 --> 00:16:33.660
Well, Renge-chan, I'll see you tomorrow.

00:16:33.660 --> 00:16:35.460
See you tomorrow.

00:16:56.440 --> 00:16:58.020
I'm going out to play!

00:16:58.290 --> 00:17:00.410
Oh, have a good time.

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:01.740
I'll be back later!

00:18:12.140 --> 00:18:14.950
Thanks for walking me home.

00:18:14.950 --> 00:18:16.600
You're welcome.

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:22.310
Honoka-chin, you're leaving tomorrow, right?

00:18:22.310 --> 00:18:23.920
Oh... Yeah.

00:18:29.330 --> 00:18:33.050
Ishikawa

00:18:29.520 --> 00:18:32.190
I-It's late! I gotta go home now!

00:18:32.190 --> 00:18:33.040
Renge-chan!

00:19:06.030 --> 00:19:08.510
Oh, morning, Ren-chon.

00:19:08.510 --> 00:19:10.250
Want some osechi?

00:19:11.230 --> 00:19:12.750
Hey, Renge.

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:15.500
Candy Store, you're here?

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:18.420
Yeah. I brought a lucky bag for you.

00:19:18.820 --> 00:19:21.880
How is that a lucky bag? 
It's just stuff you couldn't sell.

00:19:22.920 --> 00:19:24.710
Well, don't eat any, then.

00:19:24.710 --> 00:19:28.080
I mean, I never said I didn't 
want any, so I'll have some...

00:19:30.390 --> 00:19:33.630
Candy Store, can I give 
this to someone else?

00:19:34.830 --> 00:19:38.650
I already gave it to you. 
You can do what you want with it.

00:19:44.470 --> 00:19:46.960
Honoka, we're going now.

00:19:46.960 --> 00:19:48.830
O-Okay...

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:56.990
Honoka-chin!

00:19:58.790 --> 00:20:00.200
Renge-chan!

00:20:00.750 --> 00:20:02.210
You came to see me!

00:20:02.660 --> 00:20:04.630
I came to give you this!

00:20:05.250 --> 00:20:06.680
Wow, candy!

00:20:06.680 --> 00:20:09.050
I can really have all this?

00:20:09.050 --> 00:20:10.270
Yeah. It's yours.

00:20:12.800 --> 00:20:13.720
Then...

00:20:17.260 --> 00:20:18.520
I'll give you this.

00:20:18.760 --> 00:20:22.380
Wha... But those are important to you.

00:20:22.380 --> 00:20:23.890
I can't take it.

00:20:23.890 --> 00:20:26.370
No, I want you to have it.

00:20:43.230 --> 00:20:44.670
Now we match!

00:20:46.270 --> 00:20:48.390
Yeah, we match.

00:20:48.530 --> 00:20:50.990
Honoka, we need to go.

00:20:50.990 --> 00:20:52.360
Oh... Okay.

00:21:03.840 --> 00:21:06.730
Honoka-chin! Bye-bye!

00:21:10.650 --> 00:21:13.540
Yeah! Bye-bye, Renge-chan!

00:21:13.540 --> 00:21:14.700
I'll be back!

00:21:49.180 --> 00:21:52.420
I got to say goodbye this time.

00:22:01.130 --> 00:22:04.840
<b>Non Non Biyori</b>

00:22:06.720 --> 00:22:13.560
<b>That's all for today</b>

00:23:31.920 --> 00:23:33.760
To think that Kaede would...

00:23:34.370 --> 00:23:37.110
You agree, don't you, Hikage?

00:23:37.110 --> 00:23:39.740
Oh, Nii-chan's studying for entrance exams.

00:23:40.590 --> 00:23:44.470
Here, Renge. I brought you another cookie.

00:23:44.470 --> 00:23:47.030
I'm gonna be even more of an onee-san.

00:23:47.020 --> 00:23:51.030
<b>Next Time
Episode 11</b>

00:23:47.020 --> 00:23:51.030
<b>I Got Drunk and Remembered</b>

